      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\frac{5}{2x}-2?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To plot $y=\\frac{5}{2x}-2,$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n- Then, stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{5}{2}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\frac{5}{2x}.$\n\n- Translate it by $2$ units down to get the graph of $y=\\frac{5}{2x}-2.$\n\n![](images/08/08925ef549329dc44ae8dc1711f101d6a2ffbbfa2c4fa225a6d21dccc458bb00.png)"
