      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\frac{2}{x-1}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To plot $y=\\frac{2}{x-1},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/e8/e80865b0f32a5473da27b39537034bcdabee0a6c24032f41413e20518642d3f4.png)\n\n- Translate it by $1$ unit to the right to get the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{x-1}.$\n\n![](images/8f/8f2a42430ac31a559e5f85c961579aa482280bd9b69ed5d948250f5fafce21a5.png)\n\n- Then, stretch the result by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\frac{2}{x-1}.$\n\n![](images/43/4309ca72d59724e15c2e6087518983d66dd8665af5ee058a0dc13b04cdd11d5c.png)"
